			"Message": "docs(Common): Add comprehensive rustdoc documentation across all 20+ service modules\n\nEvery public module in the crate — 20+ service domains from Command through Workspace — now carries `///` doc comments on its `pub mod` declaration, describing the trait or effect it defines. Individual source files gain module-level `//!` overviews, and key functions (telemetry capture, OTLP emit, initialization, configuration, traceparent decoding) receive full parameter and behavior docs.\n\nSpecific additions:\n- All `mod.rs` files: one-line `///` doc for each submodule declaration\n- `Library.rs`: doc comments on every `pub mod` line, plus an Architecture section linking to the project-wide architecture document\n- Telemetry files: function-level docs on CaptureError, CaptureEvent, CaptureSession, Configuration, DistinctId, EmitOTLPSpan, Initialize, IsAllowed, Tier, and Traceparent\n- Effect files: module-level `//!` comments on every effect constructor\n- A trailing-comma typo fix in the EmitOTLPSpan format string\n\nThe README is concurrently restyled with GitHub badge table, funding logo table using raster-free SVG sources, and consistent 100-char line wrapping throughout.\n\nThe crate now generates rich rustdoc output with meaningful descriptions for every module, trait, and public function, improving DX for both Mountain implementors and crate browsers.",
			"SHA": "60713cd93acd8ee9a617b8c6143d6a6fd0c0971a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T00:05:46Z",
